Usage:
  velox-gen [generate] [-out dir] [-package name] [-plugin tool[:key=value,...]]... [-check] [package]
        generate the gen package of a schema package (default ./schema)
  velox-gen verify [-out dir] [-package name] [-plugin tool[:key=value,...]]... [package]
        check every generated entity's metadata
  velox-gen describe [-json] [package]
        print the entities, columns and relations of a schema package;
        with -json, the model that a plugin receives
  velox-gen version
        print the version of velox-gen, of the generated code, of the plugin
        protocol and of the model
  velox-gen migrate diff [-dir ./migrations] [-dialect d] [-name n] [-allow code[=target],...]
        [-rename-table old=new]... [-rename-column table.old=new]...
        [-lock-timeout 5s] [-check] [-dry-run] [-db dsn] [package]
        write the migration that brings the directory's schema.json to the
        schema package
  velox-gen migrate apply [-dir ./migrations] [-db dsn] [-to version] [-resume]
        [-lock-wait 5m] [-dry-run] [-baseline version]
        apply the pending migration files to the database (-db or $VELOX_DB)
  velox-gen migrate status [-dir ./migrations] [-db dsn] [-json]
        print the applied, pending, dirty and ahead versions
  velox-gen migrate drift [-dir ./migrations] [-db dsn] [-json]
        print how the database's tables differ from schema.json
  velox-gen migrate baseline [-dir ./migrations] -dialect d [-db dsn] [package]
        adopt an existing database into a new migration directory
  velox-gen migrate lint [-dir ./migrations] [-since version]
        check the migration files
  velox-gen migrate hash [-dir ./migrations] [-check]
        rewrite velox.sum
  velox-gen migrate resolve [-dir ./migrations] [-db dsn] -version n (-applied | -undone | -statements k | -adopt | -forget)
        tell the history what was done by hand
  velox-gen migrate sql -dialect postgres|mysql|sqlite [package]
        print the schema package's DDL, for Atlas's external_schema

Exit codes:
  0  success
  1  an error
  2  misuse: an unknown subcommand or flag, a malformed option
  3  stale: generated files (generate -check; verify, for a plugin's Go file),
     or the migration directory (migrate diff -check, migrate hash -check);
     pending files (migrate status); drift (migrate drift)
